{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The explicit-transfer harness completed on a clean copy (CheckRun 2b61659461634c04b53ec61c35541227, exit 0) and answered the open question with a mix I have kept precise: the named target really held no vote (target_suffrage=Nonvoter), the caller's future reported no error, yet the named target never reached Leader in the window and ended as Follower, while the cluster term moved from 2 to 4 and the only server seen leading was the original leader, in Leader state at the end. So the request was accepted and reported as done while the authority it names did not move to that server. The impossibility is source-fixed, not window-dependent: a vote-less member gets no self-vote in electSelf (a vote is cast only for servers whose suffrage is Voter), voters reject its RequestVote after adopting its higher term, and only voters start elections; the explicit path accepted it because it only looks for a replication state, whereas the implicit pickServer path deliberately skips non-voters, and the caller is told \"no error\" because losing leadership during a transfer answers nil. Reading the run's own retained DEBUG log then turned the reconstructed sequence into an observed one: the target enters candidate state at term=3 with no pre-vote success line and asks all three voters for a vote while never logging a self-vote, each voter logs term adoption immediately followed by 'rejecting vote request since node is not a voter', the original leader then campaigns at term=4 (pre-vote tally 2 of votesNeeded 2) and re-enters leader state, and the same log names the lost-leadership branch for the future. I recorded the witnessed fact, answered the gap, asserted the scoped defect with its conditions, and kept three counterweights and three limits, including that no same-window control exists for the term movement - so the newly queued control case runs the identical transfer path with a voter as the target, tagged as a separate event, to separate 'the mechanism does not work here' from 'the mechanism works and a vote-less target cannot take leadership'. The three-node configuration-index and shutdown findings from earlier turns remain recorded and witnessed; this turn added no claim beyond what the receipt and log support.\"}"}}
